  "configuration_id": "config_013",
  "reason": "Existing evidence shows RNA-only models are much stronger than the only tested image-only model, with config_010 (image-only resnet50, singleprofile) at 0.208 accuracy, while the best RNA-only setup reaches about 0.653. This leaves important uncertainty about whether the image modality can be useful at all, or whether the poor result is mainly due to the weak image encoder. config_013 tests image-only with a stronger imagenet_vit_l encoder while keeping singleprofile and no aggregation/fusion, directly comparing against config_010 to isolate the effect of image representation. This is the best next experiment because it reduces uncertainty about the image modality before spending budget on more complex multimodal fusion, and it avoids changing multiple design choices simultaneously."
}

